/* ==========================================================================
   device.js — works out what the app is running on, with nothing to set up:
     tv     Samsung TVs: the remote-control layout
     touch  Android phones, tablets and car screens: the finger layout
   LG and Android TVs (Sony ...) (and index.html?dev=remote) use the new layout too, with the remote:
   remote() is then true, the page is enlarged for viewing from the sofa and
   tvnav.js moves a highlight with the arrows.
   and for touch screens how big the screen is right now:
     phone   the short side is under 600 (and the long side under 1000)
     tablet  everything bigger, car screens included
   The result is written on <html> as classes (dev-tv / dev-touch,
   size-phone / size-tablet, land / port, short) so the styles can follow it.
   For testing in a browser: index.html?dev=phone | tablet | tv | remote
   ========================================================================== */
